**Complexity**:  
- **Time**: $O(N \cdot I)$ for $N$ vertices. $I \approx 3\text{--}5$ (Vincenty iterations per edge). Spherical excess is $O(N)$ with trivial constant factor.  
- **Space**: $O(N)$ for vertex storage and edge results.  
- **Numerics**: Authalic projection preserves area exactly. L'Huilier's theorem on the auxiliary sphere guarantees $\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)$ relative error for spherical excess down to $10^{-12}$ steradians ($\sim 10\text{ m}^2$). Vincenty inverse provides millimetric perimeter/azimuth accuracy. No catastrophic cancellation observed in polar zones.

